# Rift Versioning and Release Workflow

## Version Format

**YYYY.MM.DD+<git-short-hash>**

Example: `2026.01.02+cfc5e46`

This format:
- Matches the versioning shown on myrift.dev website
- Is automatically generated before each package build
- Includes the git commit hash for traceability

## Automatic Version Generation

The version is automatically updated when you run any release or package command.
The script `scripts/update-version.js` generates the version from the current date and git commit.

## Release Workflow

### One Command Release

Single command does everything:

```bash
bun run release        # Full release to GitHub
bun run release:dry    # Preview without publishing
```

This automatically:
0. **Runs evals** (release gate - blocks if pass rate < 70%)
1. Builds DMG with current version
2. Generates SHA256 checksum for download verification
3. Creates changelog from git commits since last release
4. Publishes GitHub Release with DMG + checksum attached
5. Commits and pushes version bump to git
6. Verifies release is live
7. **Publishes evals** to https://myrift.dev/evals

### Evals Integration

Every release is tied to eval results:
- Evals must pass (≥70%) before release proceeds
- Eval results are tagged with the release version
- Website shows version selector to compare historical releases
- Run `bun run evals:export` to manually update website evals

### What Gets Published

- **GitHub Release**: `github.com/mkmk10k/rift/releases` (public repo — download links work)
- **Artifacts**: 
  - `Rift-{version}-arm64.dmg` - macOS installer
  - `Rift-{version}-arm64.dmg.sha256` - Checksum file
- **Release Notes**: Auto-generated from git commits

### After Release: Sync Public Source

After running `bun run release`, sync the source code to the public repo:

```bash
bun run publish-public
```

This keeps the open-source code on `mkmk10k/rift` in sync with the release.
See `.publish-ignore` for what gets excluded (website, internal scripts, etc.).

### Dry Run First

Always preview before publishing:

```bash
bun run release:dry
```

This shows:
- What version will be released
- What files will be uploaded
- What changelog will be generated
- No actual changes are made

## Manual Build (Without Release)

If you just need to build without releasing:

```bash
bun run package        # Full package (DMG + ZIP)
bun run package:dmg    # DMG only
bun run package:zip    # ZIP only
```

Output directory: `dist-package/`

## Update Checking

Users can check for updates from the app's tray menu:
- **Check for Updates...** → Fetches latest from GitHub Releases API
- If newer version found, downloads DMG and reveals in Finder

The update service uses the same GitHub releases that `bun run release` creates.

## Prerequisites

GitHub CLI must be installed and authenticated (one-time setup):

```bash
brew install gh
gh auth login
```

## Important Notes

- **Never manually edit the version in package.json** - use `bun run version`
- The version is tied to the git commit hash at build time
- Rebuilding on a different commit will produce a different version
- The DMG filename includes the version for easy identification

## Code Signing (Future)

Currently the app is **not notarized**. For smoother user experience:
- Apple Developer Program membership ($99/year) required
- Add signing configuration to electron-builder
- Notarize before distribution

Users currently must right-click → Open on first launch.
